// expect: 42
// A PARAMETER SPELLED LIKE AN EFFECT OP BECOMES A PERFORM. `get` is
// `apply`'s parameter, bound to `inc`, so `get(x)` is 42. The module does
// not assemble (measured 2026-09-25: values remaining on the stack) while
// `mentl check` is clean: lowering asks the environment what `get` is before
// it asks the scope, and the environment answers with the op.
//
// Retires when lowering dispatches on the declaration a call resolves to,
// never on its spelling (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
effect Get {
  get() -> Int
}

handler give {
  get() => resume(5),
}

fn apply(get, x) = get(x)

fn inc(n) = n + 1

fn main() = (apply(inc, 41)) ~> give
